/T (Ion sources: Heated filament emits electrons \(thermionic emission\), which ignite an arc discharge in helium gas and create a plasma. A magnet around the source compresses the plasma, and ions are extracted by a fixed extraction voltage and a 40 kV pre-acceleration. This project looks at the second source \(S2\) intended for producing Helium isotopes.)
/E (Ion sources: Heated filament emits electrons \(thermionic emission\), which ignite an arc discharge in helium gas and create a plasma. A magnet around the source compresses the plasma, and ions are extracted by a fixed extraction voltage and a 40 kV pre-acceleration. This project looks at the second source \(S2\) intended for producing Helium isotopes.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [308]
>>
