336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 19 0 R
/T (The duoplasmatron ion sources at Uppsala Universities Tandem laboratory deliver around 70% of the scheduled beam time, making their reliable operation critical for scientific output. However, the chaotic nature of plasma combined with the high parameter-space used to operate lead to long-term instabilities, day-to-day shifts in optimal settings and poor reproducibility. Despite these limitations duplasmatron sources remain widely used at small and medium-scale accelerator laboratories due to lack of practical alternatives [1].)
/E (The duoplasmatron ion sources at Uppsala Universities Tandem laboratory deliver around 70% of the scheduled beam time, making their reliable operation critical for scientific output. However, the chaotic nature of plasma combined with the high parameter-space used to operate lead to long-term instabilities, day-to-day shifts in optimal settings and poor reproducibility. Despite these limitations duplasmatron sources remain widely used at small and medium-scale accelerator laboratories due to lack of practical alternatives [1].)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [316]
>>
endobj
337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 19 0 R
/T (The high-parameter space and chaotic dynamics of ion sources has made machine learning alternatives toward automation increasingly researched. This seed project took the first steps  toward AI-assisted operation of Tandems duoplasmatron ion source by implementing a structured database for relevant control parameters and readout values and investigated beam stablity and intensity correlation to the operator parameters using classification and regression models.)
/E (The high-parameter space and chaotic dynamics of ion sources has made machine learning alternatives toward automation increasingly researched. This seed project took the first steps  toward AI-assisted operation of Tandems duoplasmatron ion source by implementing a structured database for relevant control parameters and readout values and investigated beam stablity and intensity correlation to the operator parameters using classification and regression models.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [317]
>>
endobj
